{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And he put a veil over his face.</b> Because everyone was gazing at him, and Moses was exceedingly humble and bashful, and he would feel ashamed that they were gazing at the horns of light of his face — for such is the disposition of everyone who is bashful — therefore he put a veil over his face to cover the eyes of onlookers. But when he came before HaShem to learn Torah from His mouth, then he needed to remove the veil of shame from his face, for the bashful one cannot learn (Avot 2:6). Therefore it says: ״וּבְבֹא מֹשֶׁה לִפְנֵי ה׳ לְדַבֵּר אִתּוֹ יָסִיר הַמַּסְוֶה עַד צֵאתוֹ״."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:25:11.922414203Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}